{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>Do not dishevel.</b> Do not let the hair grow long — from here a mourner is forbidden to cut his hair. But you must not mix up the joy of the Omnipresent (Mo'ed Katan 14)." "<b>And you shall not die.</b> Thus if you do, you will die (Sifra)." "<b>And your brothers, the whole house of Israel.</b> From here, the bereavement of Torah scholars is imposed upon all to mourn over it (Mo'ed Katan 28)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:05:37.685814257Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}